# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KuruGrid environment — Monad MAINNET
#
# Copy to `.env.local` (git-ignored). Every value here is PUBLIC / client-side.
# KuruGrid is a zero-backend app: nothing here is a secret.
#
# !! READ BEFORE COMMITTING ANY URL BELOW !!
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` variables are inlined into the JavaScript bundle and are
# therefore readable by anyone who loads the page. That is fine for an RPC URL
# and fine for a public contract address. It is NOT fine for a private key,
# and it is NOT fine for a provider URL that embeds an API key in its path —
# QuickNode-style URLs (`…quiknode.pro/<64-hex-key>/`) leak that key to every
# visitor. Keep key-bearing URLs in `.env.local` only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Kuru CLOB ORDERBOOK (market) contract for MON/USDC on Monad Mainnet.
#
# This is the ORDERBOOK address — NOT the USDC token address. Pointing this at
# the USDC token is the most damaging mistake available here: that address has
# contract code, so a `getCode` check passes, but it is not an orderbook and the
# market read fails with "no orderbook here" instead of a useful error.
#
#   Orderbook : 0x065C9d28E428A0db40191a54d33d5b7c71a9C394
#   USDC token: 0x754704Bc059F8C67012fEd69BC8A327a5aafb603   (do not use here)
#
# Leave unset to fall back to the zero-address sentinel, which fails fast with a
# remediation rather than broadcasting into a market nobody chose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_KURU_MARKET_ADDRESS=0x065C9d28E428A0db40191a54d33d5b7c71a9C394

# Read-only RPC used for telemetry, orderbook reads and market params.
# Optional — defaults to MONAD_MAINNET.rpcUrls[0] in lib/constants.ts.
#
# If you paste a QuickNode/Ankr URL here, remember it ships to the browser. Use
# a public endpoint, or a provider key you are willing to expose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MONAD_RPC_URL=https://rpc.monad.xyz

# Optional WebSocket endpoint for the per-block live feed.
# Unset = HTTP polling only, which is fully functional. Never a private key.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MONAD_WSS_URL=wss://your-endpoint.quiknode.pro/<your-api-key>/